# Bazel configuration for the agent, mounted at /home/openclaw/.bazelrc.
#
# Keep Bazel's output base and disk cache on the ephemeral /bazel-cache emptyDir,
# never the persistent state PVC. Without this the agent accreted output bases
# under .openclaw/workspace/.cache/bazel-* -- ~100GiB of regenerable build
# artifacts on a claim whose real state is under 2GiB, which is what made the
# gateway's SQLite reads compete with SeaweedFS compaction on a saturated HDD.
# haku-openclaw-spike hit the same thing first (a single run left a 65G output
# base) and fixed it the same way.
#
# Ephemeral means re-fetched per pod start; the volume's sizeLimit caps runaway
# growth so a bad build evicts the pod rather than filling the node disk.
#
# Gotcha: this sets the *default* only. The bases found on the PVC came from the
# agent passing an explicit --output_user_root per project, which overrides an
# rc file. Keeping builds off the PVC also needs the agent not to redirect them
# back; see ../TOOLING.md.
startup --output_user_root=/bazel-cache/output
build --disk_cache=/bazel-cache/disk
